  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A setting or feature that when toggled, makes you inherently invisible to viewers in regards to model data, avatar data, etc.\nPut simply it would allow you to appear as a robot indefinitely to everyone but friends, or everyone up to a certain trust level. In this state of existence, it would seem as though you’re basically a blank slate. Users wouldn’t be able to see your model nor any meaningful data to allow stealing of said avatar.\nInteraction would still be allowed, meaning casual conversation and all that good stuff could still occur.\nThe reason I’m suggesting this is due to the sheer amount of time and money I have put in to some of my avatars, and I’m sure that streamers or big creators would be no different. I’m scared to go anywhere aside from places I trust with friends.\nIt makes meeting new people quite difficult.\nThis could be a VRChat+ Feature, or an additional paid protection feature if need be.",
